  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating skewness based on the portion of probability assigned to favorable outcomes. The individual explicitly noted that the chance in Lottery B is twice as high as in Lottery A, which directly corresponds to the greater probability mass on the favorable outcome in B. This matches the definition of left-skewness used in the reason: a greater portion of probability on favorable outcomes. The individual’s justification—'the chance is twice as high'—is consistent with the rule of the decision reason: preferring the lottery with more probability mass on the favorable outcome (i.e., more left-skewed). The information considered by the individual (probabilities of favorable outcomes) and the justification (higher chance = better) align exactly with the decision reason. Therefore, the individual used the skewness-based reason to make the decision.",
  "final_assessment_score": 100
